       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg, and the usual starting dose is 2.5\u20135 mg. Nothing in what you've told me (normal kidney and liver function, 70 kg) would justify a dose that high. Doses above the maximum raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily (the maximum dose)\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily (the typical starting or maintenance dose)\n- **3 mg**, or some other dose, if the 30 was a typo\n\nIf you do want 30 mg, tell me and I'll enter it. A short note with the clinical rationale would help pharmacy and nursing verify it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
